## SEVERITY / VERDICT (the grading rule is decided HERE; apply it, do not re-argue it)
*Blocker:* a path beyond the one; a product byte; a removed or edited existing line; the new row RED with the product unmutated; the head moved (a verdict is valid only at the head it ran on); a retained kill gone green because of the added row; a reproduced timing red (3 of 3 alone at the head, not at main); a NEW CodeQL alert at or above the ruleset's thresholds on the changed lines; a secret; a person's name, decision-card id, ticket key or mutant id in an added line or the commit message; a build warning (warnings-as-errors); a failing test at the head after the file is re-run alone twice and the red not reproduced at main. *Major (class "a pinned row that does not turn red under the defect it names, or turns red for another reason, or can fail only by timing"; REPORTED for a product-owner card, not a build round):* the new row GREEN under m1, m2, m3 or m4 (the repeated sentence listed fewer times); the new row red under a mutant only for a reason other than the list; the new row red 1 or more of 5 alone at load1 below 7; a builder claim contradicted by measurement with a verdict consequence (for example the listed delta is not exactly the 2 names, or 3158/3160 does not reproduce); a path shared with a live lane or another open PR. *Minor/Note:* the "rows added 2" wording against one source row and two listed names when the measurement agrees (THE DISCREPANCY, graded above); a PR body naming the ticket key; a PR title that differs from the commit subject; a PR body line that is stale at landing; the base test file already killing m1; cw-weak behaving differently from the builder's wording (the builder disclosed it); unsigned commits; the Co-Authored-By trailer; CodeQL PENDING at the verdict; the lineage equivalents not re-run; Linux differences you cannot run. Say which rule you applied for every finding. **Round 1 of 2: do not pad a Note into a NO GO and do not soften a Blocker: quote the plant, the row and the number.** **VERDICT RULES.** GO needs Checks 1-4, 6 and 8 measured with their controls, the new row red under every one of m1-m4 and GREEN at c0 and at the BASE product, the base test file GREEN under m1, zero findings above Note, CI predicate read, and every `Analyze (<language>)` run COMPLETE with the PR's open alerts zero (control fired); GO WITH FINDINGS = Minor/Note/Condition only (including an open item named on the line above the last line); NO GO on any Blocker or Major of this PR, with the class named, "round 1 of 2" and the fix-shape in prose. A security-shaped finding you cannot classify is a STOP (hand to G1).
**First line of STATUS (the verdict line; at Step 0 the placeholder `GATE VERDICT B829: PENDING`; verdict form, ONE line):** `GATE VERDICT B829: PR #129 b821/mps-walk-cap-rows <GO|GO WITH FINDINGS|NO GO> @ 09cea7d (round 1 of 2 on class "a pinned row that does not turn red under the defect it names", NO GO 0 before this gate on this PR - delta <1 commit, 1 path, +13 -0, removed lines 0 y/n; product blobs equal y/n; pure insertion y/n; hygiene y/n> - names <source rows 1 y/n; listed base n, head n; lost n, added n; discrepancy graded Note|Major> - Pass A <m1 green against the base file y/n> - Pass B <new row red under m1 m2 m3 m4 n of 4; reach m5 m6 m7 m8 n of 4; head row red unmutated 0 y/n; first failing assertion = list compare y/n> - controls <c0 y/n, c1 y/n, c2 y/n, c-fail y/n, cw-weak (a) <red|green> (b) <red|green>> - retained kills <g01 g04 g06 red n of 3> - Api <base n/n head n/n failed n skipped n> - stability <row alone n of 5 green; class 3 of 3; TZ/culture y/n> - CI <predicate read; local green y/n; Engine/Import/Api e/i/a failed n skipped n warnings n; wall s> - merge <tree = head tree y/n; conflicts n> - overlap <n shared with a live lane> - gitleaks rc <n> - CodeQL <analyses n complete of n, open alerts n, read at hh:mm>)`. Then the sections: Step 0 (sha256s, slot count), REFUSE counts, PINS (start, mid, verdict), instrument and load, PRIOR WORK, predictions with evidence paths, Checks 1-9 each with the FAIL clock and evidence path, the mutant matrix (mutant, edit, anchor count, test file base/head, predicted red set, actual red set BY NAME with first failing line, the builder's claim beside yours), the row -> credited killers table, the names table (static, run-time, trx), the Api and CI tables, the merge and overlap tables, the builder-claims table (claim, your number, agree y/n), findings `B829-n` each with severity, class, rule applied, `path:line` at the head, instrument, FAIL met, fix-shape in prose, evidence class (MEASURED AT RUNTIME / PROBED / READ ONLY), **FOR TUESDAY** (the verdict in plain words with the class and round; whether the head-pinned squash can go, with the exact command above; what is required first: every check green and CodeQL complete with zero open alerts at the moment of the merge; the candidate decisions: the READY-line wording "rows added 2", the PR body's stale "pending" sentence and the ticket key in it; that a Major of the capped class is carded, not rebuilt), FOUND / TESTED / HOW / NOT TESTED / corrections / processes, slots, trees and ports left, **UNMEASURED last** (at least: the hosted run beyond its conclusions; the Linux runner; CodeQL beyond the analyses' own counts; mutants and plants you cut; a moved main). **Last line, exactly one of:** `VERDICT: B829 PR #129 @ 09cea7d <GO|GO WITH FINDINGS|NO GO> (round 1 of 2) on main <sha7>` (main by `git ls-remote` at verdict; the findings ids with severities, the class and the CodeQL state sit on the line above it; the line carries none of the words that name a landing), or `STOPPED: NEEDS TUESDAY <one question>`.
